tell them what it's about several ministers had to break their holidays to

01:19:57.480 --> 01:19:59.870
fly to London after the meeting the

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:09.220
The following communique was issued, Her Majesty's government has been aware for some time of the passage of an increasing number of orbital vehicles, possibly missiles, over these islands.

01:20:10.660 --> 01:20:16.420
The vehicles, which are of unknown but terrestrial origin, pass over at great speed and at great height.

01:20:18.040 --> 01:20:29.510
Although there is no immediate cause for alarm, Her Majesty's government points out that they constitute a deliberate infringement of our national airspace, and steps are being taken to intercept and identify them.

01:20:30.440 --> 01:20:33.750
Now they know what it's about. Anything fresh, Bernadette?

01:20:33.890 --> 01:20:35.330
No, sir. We're still waiting on Gears.

01:20:35.770 --> 01:20:38.180
The director at Thorness. The machine and the goals.

01:20:38.240 --> 01:20:40.790
That's our best hope, I suppose. Do you think it'll work?

01:20:40.970 --> 01:20:44.090
It is working, sir. We've got to find our own answers.

01:20:45.480 --> 01:20:48.980
We'll be like Belgium in 1914 or Czechoslovakia in 38.

01:20:49.690 --> 01:20:53.670
Berlin in 61. By the time our allies get round to it, we'll be sunk.

01:20:53.910 --> 01:20:55.410
We're going as fast as we can, sir.

01:20:55.840 --> 01:20:57.400
What's General Van der Berg going?

01:20:57.580 --> 01:20:59.400
He's at Baldershaw Fell, the radio telescope.

01:20:59.540 --> 01:20:59.740
Why?

01:21:00.220 --> 01:21:01.360
With Reinhardt, watching the traces.

01:21:01.620 --> 01:21:04.340
It's no good watching them. We've got to do something about them.

01:21:05.520 --> 01:21:07.060
They've been coming over thick and fast.

01:21:08.160 --> 01:21:10.320
We've had 102 of them so far.

01:21:10.600 --> 01:21:11.320
What's that one, Harvey?

01:21:11.720 --> 01:21:12.760
Number 103, Professor.

01:21:13.370 --> 01:21:15.710
Height about 350 miles, course 265...

01:21:15.710 --> 01:21:17.110
Any change in characteristics?

01:21:17.470 --> 01:21:19.230
No, they just come over.

01:21:20.130 --> 01:21:24.310
They're launched, we think, from about 40 north by 130 to 135 east.

01:21:24.390 --> 01:21:25.470
That's as near as we can estimate.

01:21:26.140 --> 01:21:29.980
Somewhere between Manchuria, Vladivostok and Northern Ireland of Japan.

01:21:30.790 --> 01:21:35.680
So, could it be any of three fellow members of the United Nations?

01:21:35.980 --> 01:21:37.920
Is the West taking this to the Security Council?

01:21:38.080 --> 01:21:40.200
Not until we can negotiate through strength.

01:21:40.460 --> 01:21:42.180
We've got to have some means of defense first.

01:21:42.740 --> 01:21:44.900
I don't see what their point is.

01:21:45.020 --> 01:21:49.040
The point is, somebody in the East wants us to know they've got the technical edge on us.

01:21:49.040 --> 01:21:53.300
So they launch a whole series of uninterceptable missiles.

01:21:53.680 --> 01:21:59.280
They flaunt them over our heads just to show the world that we have no means of retaliation.

01:22:00.350 --> 01:22:02.610
It's just another form of saber-raptor.

01:22:02.950 --> 01:22:06.930
They'd love us to go squealing to the United Nations and admit our weakness.

01:22:07.500 --> 01:22:08.620
Then they'd have us.

01:22:09.500 --> 01:22:11.980
But maybe we won't need to admit any weakness.

01:22:12.320 --> 01:22:13.120
What's Gears doing?

01:22:13.480 --> 01:22:15.440
Oh, he's going as fast as he can.

01:22:15.620 --> 01:22:16.400
With the computer?

01:22:16.660 --> 01:22:17.300
And the creature.

01:22:17.620 --> 01:22:18.820
Do you think that's safe?

01:22:19.120 --> 01:22:20.940
This is not a safe world.

01:22:21.180 --> 01:22:23.180
Well, there are two schools of thought.

01:22:23.480 --> 01:22:25.250
Yeah, yours and ours.

01:22:25.410 --> 01:22:27.290
Oh, I don't feel sure about it like Fleming does.

01:22:27.860 --> 01:22:29.370
Just uneasy.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:30.920
Is Fleming still worrying you?

01:22:31.120 --> 01:22:32.160
No, he just sits around.

01:22:32.560 --> 01:22:33.740
Hmm, that doesn't sound...

01:22:33.740 --> 01:22:34.800
A very stable solution.

01:22:35.160 --> 01:22:37.140
He's only trying to save face, if you ask me.

01:22:37.600 --> 01:22:38.780
He knows he's made a lot of trouble,

01:22:39.020 --> 01:22:40.500
and doesn't like to admit he's been in the wrong.

01:22:40.720 --> 01:22:41.980
Well, let me know if you have any difficulty.

01:22:42.400 --> 01:22:43.040
We will.

01:22:43.180 --> 01:22:43.660
And the creature?

01:22:43.880 --> 01:22:44.660
Oh, she's all right.

01:22:45.010 --> 01:22:46.950
I give her a medical check of her once a day.

01:22:47.150 --> 01:22:48.350
She's not showing signs of strain?

01:22:48.590 --> 01:22:48.770
No.

01:22:49.110 --> 01:22:50.970
No, it all seems quite effortless to her.

01:22:51.340 --> 01:22:53.440
She takes the calculations your people give her,

01:22:53.880 --> 01:22:54.940
communicates them to the computer,

01:22:55.100 --> 01:22:56.040
and comes up with the results.

01:22:56.570 --> 01:22:57.830
At least, I hope they're the results.

01:22:58.090 --> 01:22:58.530
More then.

01:22:58.670 --> 01:22:59.850
They're telling us what to do now.

01:23:00.440 --> 01:23:01.260
Is that what you want?

01:23:01.750 --> 01:23:02.370
It makes sense.

01:23:18.060 --> 01:23:19.200
Why don't you give up, John?

01:23:19.870 --> 01:23:20.090
Me?

01:23:20.620 --> 01:23:21.420
Why don't you leave?

01:23:22.610 --> 01:23:23.730
That'd please you, wouldn't it?

01:23:24.240 --> 01:23:25.420
It would not please me.

01:23:25.980 --> 01:23:28.460
But there's nothing you can do eating your heart out here.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:31.500
It's a nice little three-handed game, isn't it?

01:23:32.440 --> 01:23:34.630
I watch her, you watch me.

01:23:34.870 --> 01:23:36.230
You're not doing yourself any good.

01:23:37.710 --> 01:23:38.090
Jealous?

01:23:39.030 --> 01:23:39.730
Don't be absurd.

01:23:42.190 --> 01:23:50.790
They're all so damn sure there's something I've got to find out about it or about her.

01:23:52.500 --> 01:23:53.160
I'll stick around.

01:23:53.320 --> 01:23:53.860
But John...

01:23:53.860 --> 01:23:55.400
You'll have to get a warrant to throw me out.

01:23:55.560 --> 01:23:57.340
I don't want to throw you out.

01:23:59.300 --> 01:23:59.980
I wish to see...

01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:01.760
Can you talk to me as about these, please?

01:24:02.000 --> 01:24:02.280
No.

01:24:02.680 --> 01:24:02.920
No.

01:24:04.080 --> 01:24:04.920
I'll see this, please.

01:24:12.590 --> 01:24:13.450
...in your work.

01:24:15.360 --> 01:24:16.760
You're quite indispensable, aren't you?

01:24:16.920 --> 01:24:18.460
